A photorealistic aerial view of Brunei's capital at golden hour, showing the iconic Omar Ali Saifuddien Mosque with its golden dome reflected in the lagoon, while streams of glowing fiber optic cables and digital data particles flow like rivers through the streets, weaving between traditional Malay stilt houses and modern glass buildings. Young professionals in business attire walk along waterfront promenades, their silhouettes casting long shadows. Flocks of birds transform into abstract digital nodes as they rise into the amber sky, symbolizing the migration and mobility of talent. The scene captures the tension between tradition and technological transformation, with warm tropical light filtering through scattered clouds over the South China Sea.
